Maybe better to make panel-actions sticky at bottom? But then would overlay content. Or make draw panel scroll clearly (it does). User can scroll. But build button should be easily reachable. At 768 height it's fine; at 720, bottom cut ~? client 616 vs 691 -> 75 cut; panel actions h101 + microcopy 36 => build button likely partly or fully visible? Content order ends: panel-actions 101 then microcopy 36. From bottom, 75 cut means microcopy 36 + 39 of panel-actions, so the lower part of example button and maybe half of build? Actually panel-actions has build first then example. Cutting 39 from bottom cuts example partially, build visible. So build always visible. That's acceptable.

Could reduce further by hiding microcopy at short heights via media query `(max-height: 780px) { .microcopy { display:none } }`, which would save 36 and make fit at 768. That's a nice targeted solution. At 768 we currently cut 27 = only microcopy, so hiding it fits. At 720 still cut 39 from action area; maybe hide `.panel-copy` too for short heights? Or reduce. Add:
