content.text:
Now add sticker group and API. Need choose anchor positions. Also need part setter and livery state. Let's patch return block. Current return block from 550. We'll replace with extended.

Need add sticker group before root.traverse? Can add after wheels/nose decal; it doesn't matter. Add:
```
  const stickerGroup = new THREE.Group();
  body.add(stickerGroup);

  const partMaterials = { ... };
  function clearStickerGroup() {...}
  function setStickers(next = {}) { ... }
  setStickers(livery?.stickers || {});
```
But `root.traverse` sets castShadow true for all meshes, including stickers, which would cast weird shadows. We can set castShadow false after in setStickers or move traverse before stickers. Easier: create sticker group after root.traverse but before return. But sticker group added to body after traverse; its meshes have castShadow false in makeStickerPlane. Great. Do that.

- `clearStickerGroup` disposes materials:
```
for (const child of stickerGroup.children.slice()) {
  stickerGroup.remove(child);
  child.geometry?.dispose();
  if (child.material) { child.material.map?.dispose(); child.material.dispose(); }
}
```
- `setStickers` uses body color ink:
```
const ink = readableInk(paintMat.color);
const stickers = next || {};
...
```
- Need read side sticker positions maybe conflict with existing side decal. Let's place side sticker at z=-0.85, y=0.5. Check sidepod shape: sphere scale z .94 centered -0.35 => spans -1.29..0.59; at z=-0.85 the sphere cross-section width smaller; x outer ~0.55 + 0.36*sqrt(1 - (0.5/0.94)^2) ≈ 0.55+0.30=0.85. Our x .918 may float slightly. Could use .86. Existing decal at z=-0.38 x .902. At z -0.38, outer ~.91. For sticker at z -0.75, outer ~.89. Use x ±0.885, y .48, z -0.72. The plane size .68x.24. If x is too far out, floating. Fine.
- Nose sticker at z 1.62 y .56. Let's use 0.56. Existing nose number z1.28, might extend 0.19 along z; sticker at 1.62 no overlap.
- Wing sticker at z -2.08 y 1.215. The rear wing main is horizontal-ish rotation 0.12. Plane rotation x=-PI/2; if wing plane is tilted around x by 0.12, need rotate `-Math.PI/2 + 0.12`? Let's think: plane default lies in XY plane facing +Z. Rotating x=-PI/2 makes it lie in XZ plane facing +Y. Rear wing main itself is BoxGeometry, rotated x=+0.12 (tilting). To match, plane rotation.x = -PI/2 + 0.12? A rotation of +0.12 around X tilts its normal; yes use -PI/2 + 0.12. Positioned y 1.215, z -2.12. Good.
- Sticker group object maybe name `stickers`.

Part materials:
```
const partMaterials = { body: paintMat, frontWing: frontWingMat, rearWing: rearWingMat, trim: accentMat, helmet: helmetMat, wheels: wheelMat };
```
- `setPart(part, value)`:
```
const mat = partMaterials[part]; if (!mat) return false;
mat.color.set(value);
if (part === 'wheels') mat.emissive.set(value);
if (part === 'body') { paint = mat.color.getHex(); decal? existing decals won't update ink; okay. }
return true;
```
No need update decals on body change; side/nose decal colors won't change, but okay.
- `setPaint` calls `setPart('body', value)`.
- `getPart(part)` maybe.
- `setStickers`.

Return `setPart`, `setStickers`, `partMaterials` maybe not.

Also if `livery.stickers` present at creation, apply after traverse. Good.
- `stickerGroup` not included in root.traverse dispose? setStickers replaced and disposed, final dispose traverses root incl group. Good.

Let's patch.

