Now responsive updates. At max-width 1180: dock body gap 22, maybe 3 cols still. At 900: currently grid-template-columns 1fr; with three panels stack, tall. We could make 2 columns at <=900 and one at small. But mobile 390 width -> one column. Stickers is compact.

At <=900 set `.garage-dock-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }` and stickers span 2? Hmm stage copy etc. At 900, garage dock will be tall (parts row, two columns, footer hidden). Fine.

At <=760, one column. Need `.garage-stickers-panel` maybe grid-column: span 2 at 900. Let's do:

@media max-width 900:
```
.garage-dock-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
.garage-stickers-panel { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
.garage-parts-row { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
```
At max-width 760:
```
.garage-dock-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
.garage-stickers-panel { grid-column: auto; }
```
But with screen fixed height and dock large, stage shrinks maybe negative? Grid rows auto 1fr auto; 1fr minimum auto can overflow. Could make #screen-garage overflow-y auto on mobile. Better.

Let's edit responsive.

